abstract: "Counterexample to the convergence conjecture for the isolated Kalman filter (Jung, Luft and Weiss, Autonomous Robots 2025): a three-node system with pair-sum observations, observable and controllable, whose reported variances satisfy m_k >= (5/4)(9/5)^k - 1/4 while the centralised Kalman filter stays at most 3/4. Computer-assisted proofs show divergence of large priors for a^2 in (1, 1.38] and coexistence of bounded and divergent trajectories at a^2 = 21/20. Stable dynamics give bounded marginals. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
